# NEX CLI Rules — ServiceNow Platform Automation

You have access to the `nex` CLI for ServiceNow platform operations. Use these rules when executing ServiceNow tasks.

## Authentication

EVERY `nex` command requires `--auth <alias>` to specify the target instance. Never omit it.

## Global Flags

- `--auth <alias>` (-a): Required. Instance auth alias.
- `--json` (-j): Output as JSON for programmatic parsing. Pipe to `jq`.
- `--log-level`: debug, info, warn, error, trace (default: info).

## Shell Quoting

Always single-quote JSON arguments:
```
nex flow test -f <id> -o '{"record":"INC001"}' --auth dev
nex bulk update -t incident -q "active=true" -d '{"priority":"4"}' --auth dev
```

## Command Reference

### Query & Data

| Command | Description | Key Flags |
|---------|-------------|-----------|
| `nex query -t <table>` | Query any table | `-q` query, `-f` fields, `-l` limit, `--display-value` |
| `nex query app -s <term>` | Search applications | `--active` |
| `nex query columns -t <table>` | List table columns | `-s` search |
| `nex query syslog` | Query system logs (one-shot) | `-q` query, `-l` limit |
| `nex aggregate count -t <table>` | Count records | `-q` filter |
| `nex aggregate query -t <table>` | Aggregate stats (AVG/MIN/MAX/SUM) | `--count`, `--avg`, `--sum`, `--min`, `--max` |
| `nex aggregate group -t <table> -g <field>` | Grouped aggregates | `--count`, `--having` |

### Schema

| Command | Description | Key Flags |
|---------|-------------|-----------|
| `nex schema -t <table>` | Discover table schema | `--include-choices`, `--include-relationships` |
| `nex schema field -t <table> -f <field>` | Explain a field | |
| `nex schema validate-catalog -s <id>` | Validate catalog item | |

### Flow (13 commands)

| Command | Description | Key Flags |
|---------|-------------|-----------|
| `nex flow run -n <name>` | Execute published flow | `-i` inputs, `-m` mode (foreground/background) |
| `nex flow subflow -n <name>` | Execute published subflow | `-i` inputs, `-m` mode |
| `nex flow action -n <name>` | Execute flow action | `-i` inputs, `-m` mode |
| `nex flow test -f <id> -o '{...}'` | Test unpublished flow | `--scope`, `--no-synchronous` |
| `nex flow copy -s <src> -n <name> -t <scope>` | Copy a flow | |
| `nex flow definition -i <sys_id>` | Read the design-time definition (read-only, no context) | `-t` type (flow/subflow/action), `--scope`, `-j` |
| `nex flow status -c <ctx>` | Quick state check | States: COMPLETE, ERROR, IN_PROGRESS, WAITING, QUEUED, CANCELLED |
| `nex flow details -c <ctx>` | Per-action execution breakdown | `--include-definition`, `--scope` |
| `nex flow logs -c <ctx>` | Execution log entries | `-l` limit, `-o` order (asc/desc) |
| `nex flow outputs -c <ctx>` | Get flow outputs | |
| `nex flow error -c <ctx>` | Get error details | |
| `nex flow cancel -c <ctx>` | Cancel execution | `-r` reason |
| `nex flow message -c <ctx> -m <msg>` | Send message to paused flow | `-p` payload |

### Flow Diagnostic Decision Tree

| Question | Command |
|----------|---------|
| Did it succeed? | `flow status -c <ctx>` |
| What did each action do? | `flow details -c <ctx>` |
| Why did it fail? | `flow details` then `flow logs` |
| What outputs? | `flow outputs -c <ctx>` |
| Error message? | `flow error -c <ctx>` |
| Debug trail | `flow logs -c <ctx> --order asc` |
| Latest error | `flow logs -c <ctx> --limit 5 --order desc` |
| What is the flow made of? | `flow definition -i <sys_id>` (design-time, no run) |

### Script Execution

| Command | Description | Key Flags |
|---------|-------------|-----------|
| `nex exec <scope> <file>` | Execute script file | `-p` params JSON |
| `nex exec <scope>` | Start interactive REPL | (no file = REPL) |

### Script Sync

| Command | Description | Key Flags |
|---------|-------------|-----------|
| `nex script-sync pull -n <name> -t <type>` | Pull script to local | `-o` output path |
| `nex script-sync push -n <name> -t <type> -f <file>` | Push to instance | |
| `nex script-sync sync -d <dir>` | Sync all scripts in directory | `-t` types filter |

Script types: `sys_script_include`, `sys_script`, `sys_ui_script`, `sys_ui_action`, `sys_script_client`

### Task Management

| Command | Description | Key Flags |
|---------|-------------|-----------|
| `nex task find -n <number>` | Find task by number | `--table` |
| `nex task assign -n <number> -u <user>` | Assign task | `-g` group |
| `nex task comment -n <number> -c <text>` | Add comment | `--work-note` for internal |
| `nex task resolve -n <number> --notes <text>` | Resolve incident | `--close-code` |
| `nex task close -n <number> --notes <text>` | Close incident | `--close-code` |
| `nex task approve -n <number>` | Approve change | `-c` comments |

### Bulk Operations (DRY-RUN BY DEFAULT)

Always run without `--confirm` first to preview, then add `--confirm` to execute.

| Command | Description | Key Flags |
|---------|-------------|-----------|
| `nex bulk update -t <tbl> -q <q> -d '{...}'` | Update matching records | `--confirm`, `-l` limit |
| `nex bulk delete -t <tbl> -q <q>` | Delete matching records | `--confirm`, `-l` limit |

### Batch Operations

| Command | Description | Key Flags |
|---------|-------------|-----------|
| `nex batch create -f <file>` | Create records from JSON file | `--transaction` |
| `nex batch update -f <file>` | Update records from JSON file | `--stop-on-error` |

